WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.630
- [Announcer] You've earned
this, so hold it up hot.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.582
- We turn out to the Battle of the Beer,

00:00:05.582 --> 00:00:06.958
as the Wall Street Journal reporting that

00:00:06.958 --> 00:00:08.910
Modelo has overtaken Bud
Light as America's top beer.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.230
- [Narrator] You may think Modelo

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.600
dethroned Bud Light after this.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.340
- And Bud Light sent me possibly

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.880
the best gift ever, a can
on with my face on it.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.410
- [Narrator] Led to this.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.150
- The Bud Light boycott.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.647
(gun firing)

00:00:23.647 --> 00:00:25.950
- I'll serve you anything
except Bud Light.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.930
- [Narrator] Well, that's partly true,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.910
but it's not the whole story.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.680
It's also thanks to this guy.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.700
- I had the privilege

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.730
of being President
Obama's antitrust chief.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.080
- [Narrator] He filed a lawsuit that

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.150
changed everything for the brand,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.640
putting the imported
Mexican beer on the path

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.570
to take down the king of beers, Bud Light.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.510
This is the Economics of Modelo.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.550
- [Bill] It's a world
that changes all the time

00:00:51.395 --> 00:00:53.160
but what's important never changes.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.440
- [Narrator] But change came in 2012

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.360
when Anheuser-Busch InBev looked to

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.950
merge with Groupo Modelo.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.830
the brewer of Modelo Especial, and Corona.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.820
- I started at the Justice Department

00:01:04.781 --> 00:01:07.560
in early January of 2013
and the biggest first matter

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.250
before me was an
investigation the staff had

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.560
into the effort by AB InBev to acquire

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:18.360
the worldwide rights to Modelo.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.030
- [Narrator] That year, AB
InBev maker of Bud Light,

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.330
along with MillerCoors made up about 65%

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.920
of the US beer market.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.560
- What our investigation found was that

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.560
every year InBev ABI and
MillerCoors would raise prices.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.980
Modelo kept their prices stable,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.450
and began to grow market share.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.660
They were competing on the
merits and they were winning.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.660
And it appears that AB InBev
didn't like that idea at all.

00:01:48.226 --> 00:01:49.770
- [Narrator] So the
government's antitrust lawyers

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.230
advised the world's biggest beer maker

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:55.440
it'd have to sell the US
rights to Modelo Especial.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.000
Before buying the company.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.008
- We said, you need InBev
to completely divest

00:02:01.008 --> 00:02:06.008
any interest in Modelo as it
relates to the United States.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:11.690
They thought I was crazy and
I said, "Well, I may be crazy,

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.650
but if you don't agree to
that, we're gonna sue."

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.590
And they hemmed and
hawed, And so I sued them.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.660
- [Narrator] After that,
AB InBev agreed to sell

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.110
the US rights to Modelo
Especial to Constellation.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.830
A third beverage company that
mostly sold wine and spirits

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.040
but also imported Modelo
Especial to the US.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.630
- We knew with them as an
independent owner of Modelo,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:37.140
they'd have every incentive
to grow the brand,

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.440
maintain the quality,
introduce new brands,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:44.670
incentives that InBev just
would not have had at all.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.530
- [Narrator] Modelo and
its new parent company

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.860
had a long way to go
to dethrone Bud Light.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.650
So Constellation began
looking at its marketing.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.950
- It starts with creating
that universal broad appeal

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.050
across all types of consumers

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.420
and then expanding our investment

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.560
and moving into English language

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.330
and telling that story to more people.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.980
- [Narrator] They launched a new campaign

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.203
running ads like this.

00:03:06.203 --> 00:03:08.580
- [Announcer] Modelo,
the mark of a fighter.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.310
- [Narrator] During live
multicultural sporting events

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.960
to reach new audiences.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.140
- [Commentator] The fight clock
is brought to you by Modelo.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.310
- [Narrator] Sales ticked upwards

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.620
as more people drank Modelo.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.110
And that data was presented to retailers

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:25.560
using a Constellation program
called Shopper First Shelf.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.720
- We do a lot of research
behind the scenes.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.210
We lay out the optimal
flow of the beer aisle,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.720
that will maximize retail
sales for the retailer

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.520
which then also helps
our distributor partners

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.590
and helps grow the overall beer category.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.630
- [Narrator] They said
stores could increase sales

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.270
by arranging Modelo in a vertical line

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.010
with Corona to the left.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.990
- What's interesting is Modelo

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.750
despite as big a brand as it is,

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.570
the brand awareness of Modelo is actually

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.570
much, much lower than of Corona Extra.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.040
- [Narrator] The idea was that consumers

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.590
would see Corona first
and then intuitively

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.630
look to the right and find Modelo.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.280
They also recommended that Modelo

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.900
be shelved in the refrigerators.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.060
Since most imported beer is purchased

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.310
to be consumed within six hours.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.920
So shoppers needed it cold.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.360
Inside the refrigerators,

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.294
Constellation recommended
it be placed at eye level

00:04:14.294 --> 00:04:16.500
and near the door handle.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.500
To maximize visibility,
they found beers that moved

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.640
from hinge to handle position
increased sales by 8%.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.156
- Modelo Especial has enjoyed
really high velocities

00:04:27.156 --> 00:04:28.156
for a long time.

00:04:28.156 --> 00:04:30.680
When we have really high
velocities, what's important is

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.770
that we get enough space on the shelf

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.310
so that we have enough inventory
so the shelf isn't empty.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.020
- [Narrator] Constellation
pushed retailers

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.180
for more shelf space for Modelo because

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.660
it was selling so quickly, sales rose.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.910
By the end of the 2021 calendar year,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.600
Modelo Especial had passed
AB InBev's Michelob Ultra

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.410
to land the number two spot
by retail store dollar sales.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.270
That jump was partially fueled

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.180
by a push to shift Modelo's consumer base.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.030
- In the 2019 fiscal year,

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:03.690
Modelo's consumers were
about 70% Hispanic.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.550
- [Narrator] And that
population has been growing

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.230
helping to drive sales.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.394
- But Constellation was really pushing to

00:05:09.394 --> 00:05:12.332
give the brand a mass market appeal.

00:05:12.332 --> 00:05:14.160
- [Narrator] It worked,

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.600
now about 45% of Modelo's
consumer base is non-Hispanic.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.300
Both have driven more market share.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.680
With all of that growth,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.330
analysts projected that Bud Light

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.880
was on track to lose
its top spot to Modelo

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.130
as early as 2024.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.160
But they probably didn't
anticipate Bud Light sales

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.980
falling as dramatically as they did.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.320
Anheuser-Busch says Bud
Light's US market share

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.960
has stabilized and that
it will win back drinkers

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.690
by staying away from controversial topics.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.520
Since the boycott, the company has worked

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.503
on new Bud Light ads like this,

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:51.237
emphasizing ties to
football and country music.

00:05:51.237 --> 00:05:54.830
♪ In a radio world ♪

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.632
AB InBev also said, let's not forget

00:05:58.632 --> 00:06:00.750
millions of people still
choose Bud Light each day

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.070
and year to date Bud Light remains

00:06:03.973 --> 00:06:05.220
number one in volume sales.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.140
- Modelo's Rise is really

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:10.470
the result of changing demographics,

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.800
changing consumer tastes,
and savvy marketing

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.110
on the part of Constellation.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.660
And then to sort of top it all off,

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.440
this Bud Light boycott
blew it out of the water.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.630
- We expected we would be in this position

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.220
maybe a year or two from now.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:29.220
So it did happen a little
bit earlier than expected

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.170
but it's a great place to be.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:33.600
But what we're focused on now is how

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.120
do we maintain this
position going forward?

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.210
- Now Modelo is on track to have greater

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:42.360
dollar sales for the full year of 2023.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.113
So it looks to be solidifying its place

00:06:45.113 --> 00:06:48.294
as the top beer in America.

00:06:48.294 --> 00:06:51.600
- To give the American consumer choice

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.970
is what competitive markets is all about,

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.310
and it's up to
Constellation to keep going.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.950
They clearly have the momentum and

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.683
and the consumer demand on their side.

00:07:02.551 --> 00:07:05.218
(upbeat music)

